# two closures of one literal are left unmade over one scope. One is read as a value: that read needs the literal and ends what the state holds of its own slot alone. The call of the other still takes the scope off the record that the allocation listed, and its slot is not read.
# f1 = make, f2 = run, f3 = next, f4 = peek
